      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T05:59:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "it\u0027s confusing to call this \"FWID\", as that already means something completely different (most people would think this refers to the value in the RW_FWID fmap section of the EC, which would contain the version string you see above).\n\nCan we call it \"Chrome OS version\" so that we\u0027re not reusing a term that already exists?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "842a1ff6b82f2d13685bc9860b6564ac111985ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
