      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eed5992e_593a5c9f",
        "filename": "zephyr/zmake/zmake/version.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T20:11:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree this is confusing and not ideally named. It\u0027s called `fwid` in crossystem, so the motivation was to align with that.",
      "parentUuid": "c98a2e03_8a1bf51d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 146,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "842a1ff6b82f2d13685bc9860b6564ac111985ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0880c363_5f94289f",
        "filename": "zephyr/zmake/zmake/version.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T05:59:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should be:\n\n```\nname, sep, value \u003d line.partition(\"\u003d\")\nif not sep:\n    continue\n\nname \u003d name.strip()\nvalue \u003d value.strip()\nversion_vars[name] \u003d value\n```\n\nthe difference is that if there is an \"\u003d\" after the first equals, it will be kept in the value instead of giving you a list of three+ items.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 159,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 163,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "842a1ff6b82f2d13685bc9860b6564ac111985ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
